.TH AENIGMA-VPN-DNS 8 "2026-08-12" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-vpn-dns \- configure dnsmasq DNS resolution over an OpenVPN
interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
.B \-d
.I DOMAIN
.B \-i
.I DNS_IP
.B \-f
.I INTERFACE
.RB [ \-c
.IR CNAME ]
.br
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
installs and configures
.BR dnsmasq (8)
to serve DNS on a given VPN network interface, and adds
DHCP-option push directives for DNS server and search domain to an
OpenVPN configuration file associated with
.IR DOMAIN .
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Installs the
.B dnsmasq
package via
.B apt-get
if not already present.
.IP \(bu 2
Creates (if not already present) a hosts file at
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /dnsmasq\-hosts ,
used by
.B dnsmasq
as an additional hosts source.
.IP \(bu 2
Writes a
.B dnsmasq
configuration file to
.IR /etc/dnsmasq.d/ DOMAIN .conf,
binding
.B dnsmasq
to
.I INTERFACE
and pointing it at the hosts file above. If
.B \-c
is given, also adds a
.B cname
directive mapping
.I DOMAIN
to
.IR CNAME .
This file is fully overwritten on each run.
.IP \(bu 2
Appends
.B "push \(dqdhcp-option DNS ...\(dq"
and
.B "push \(dqdhcp-option DOMAIN ...\(dq"
directives to
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
if matching directives are not already present in that file.
.IP \(bu 2
Enables and restarts
.BR dnsmasq ,
then restarts the
.B openvpn@ DOMAIN
systemd service instance so the updated configuration takes effect.
.PP
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " DOMAIN"
Domain name identifying the OpenVPN configuration to modify and the
.B dnsmasq
configuration/hosts files to create, e.g.
.IR vpn.example.com .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-i " DNS_IP"
IP address to be pushed to VPN clients as their DNS server, e.g.
.IR 10.8.0.1 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-f " INTERFACE"
Network interface
.B dnsmasq
should bind to, e.g.
.IR tun0 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-c " CNAME"
Optional. If given, configures
.B dnsmasq
to treat
.I DOMAIN
as a CNAME alias for
.IR CNAME .
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
DNS configuration was written and
.B dnsmasq
/
.B openvpn@ DOMAIN
were restarted successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or missing arguments, or the script was not run as root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /dnsmasq\-hosts
Additional hosts file consulted by
.BR dnsmasq .
Created empty if absent; its parent directory is expected to already
exist and is not created by this script.
.TP
.I /etc/dnsmasq.d/ DOMAIN .conf
Generated
.B dnsmasq
configuration for this interface/domain. Overwritten in full on each
run.
.TP
.I /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
OpenVPN configuration file. DHCP-option push directives are appended
to this file if not already present; the file itself is not created
by this script and is expected to already exist.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure DNS push and local resolution for a VPN server on
.IR tun0 :
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-vpn-dns \-d vpn.example.com \-i 10.8.0.1 \-f tun0
.EE
.RE
.PP
The same, with a CNAME alias:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-vpn-dns \-d vpn.example.com \-i 10.8.0.1 \-f tun0 \e
    \-c vpn-endpoint.example.com
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
The
.B push
directives written by this script are only meaningful in an OpenVPN
.B server
configuration; they have no effect in a
.B client
configuration. Confirm that
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
is in fact an OpenVPN server configuration for the
.I DOMAIN
given, and not a client configuration file of the same name, before
running this script against it.
.PP
The check used to decide whether to append the DNS push directive
.RB ( "grep -q \(dqdhcp-option DNS\(dq" )
matches on the directive name only, not on its value. Re-running
this script against the same
.I DOMAIN
with a different
.I DNS_IP
will therefore
.B not
update the previously pushed DNS server address; the existing
.B "push \(dqdhcp-option DNS ...\(dq"
line is left unchanged, even though the script reports the newly
requested
.I DNS_IP
as the value that was pushed. To change a previously configured DNS
push value, the corresponding line must be edited or removed from
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
manually before re-running this script.
.PP
If
.IR /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
does not already exist when this script runs, the
.B grep
check against it fails, and the subsequent
.B >>
redirection creates a new file containing only the two
.B push
directives, with none of the other OpenVPN configuration a working
server (or client) configuration requires.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnsmasq (8),
.BR openvpn (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR aenigma-vpn-client (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
